# The Dockerfile's `COPY . /opt/aw-workspace` has no filter of its own —
# without this file, ANY stray path sitting in the build context (e.g. a
# self-hosted CI runner's own checkout dir) gets baked into the image
# verbatim, .gitignore or not (.dockerignore is the only thing `docker
# build`/`podman build` actually consult).
#
# CLI credential dirs/files are the ones that mattered in practice: a
# `.claude`/`.codex`/etc left in a build runner's checkout got baked into
# an image, and every `aw-remote-host` workspace `Update()` then synced
# that baked (mostly-empty, dev-time) copy over
# /opt/aw-workspace/.claude — the exact path aw-app-agents-platform-runners'
# execute.py uses as the shared, persisted source it resyncs Workspace
# Runner CLI logins from before every spawn — silently wiping live
# credentials on every workspace update. See internal/ops/ops.go's
# syncWorkspaceSource in aw-remote-host for the matching belt-and-braces
# skip (this file prevents the bad image from ever being built in the
# first place; that skip protects hosts already running an old image that
# has one baked in).
.claude/
.claude.json
.codex/
.copilot/
.cursor/

.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.venv/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
coverage/
